  "sourceNotes": "Sukiyaki developed in Japan during the Meiji era when beef eating became more accepted after centuries of restriction. It is now a celebratory dish, eaten at New Year and on special occasions. The Kanto and Kansai regions have different methods: Kanto simmers everything in a pre-made sauce; Kansai fries the beef first and adds sugar directly.",
